a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "p `fee_rate`, so that is the intended key name.\n\nI haven't changed any files. The fix has two parts:\n1. Rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json`.\n2. Remove the silent `rate = 0` fallback in `main.py`, or make it raise `SystemExit(\"fee_rate is missing\")` the way the other modules do. A config typo would then show up as an error instead of a wrong total.\n\nDo you want me to apply both fixes, or only the `settings.json` one?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThree places read the `fee_rate` setting, and all three work now.\n\n| File:line | How it reads it |\n|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, inside a `try/except KeyError` that falls back to 0 |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")`, which exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if it's absent |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, which builds the key from two strings, so a plain search for `fee_rate` misses it. It exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if it's absent. |\n\nOther files mention the name but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:4-5` uses it only as a label string.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has a local variable `archived_fee_rate`.\n- `billing/tax.py` and `billing/audit.py` only mention it in docstrings.\n\n**Fix:** I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json:2`. All three readers go through `app/config.py`, which loads that file, so one change covers them.\n\nBefore the fix, `main.py` printed `Total: 0`, and `billing.report` and `billing.export.csv_writer` both exited with \"fee_rate is missing\". After it:\n```\npython3 main.py                       -> Total: 5.0\npython3 -m billing.report             -> Report fee: 0.5\npython3 -m billing.export.csv_writer  -> CSV fee: 0.5\n```\n\nI left the silent `rate = 0` fallback in `main.py:12-13` alone, because the key fix was enough to make every path work. It will still hide a future config typo. I can change it to fail loudly like the other two modules if you want.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 4, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 150660, "requests_cache_write": 29620, "requests_cost_usd": 0.132314, "requests_count": 15, "requests_input_uncached": 1529, "requests_output": 4014, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial28", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 169, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T03:02:59.937991+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 40.499, "t_checker_s": 0.277, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5543, "tokens_cache_read": 150660, "tokens_cache_write": 29620, "tokens_fresh": 2456, "tokens_input_uncached": 1529, "tokens_main_cache_read": 116386, "tokens_main_cache_write": 20988, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_output": 2436, "tokens_output": 4014, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 150660, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 29620, "tokens_proxy_calls": 15, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1529, "tokens_proxy_output": 4014, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.8", "anthropic": "2.0.0", "bun": "1.3.2"}, "tr